WEBVTT

00:01.980 --> 00:04.190
A long, long time ago.

00:04.400 --> 00:07.270
A story from about a hundred years ago.

00:08.070 --> 00:12.530
Nadja, guided by destiny, arrived in Italy

00:16.570 --> 00:17.870
NAAJA

00:16.570 --> 00:17.870
Nadja,

00:17.990 --> 00:20.540
With your eyes

00:17.990 --> 00:20.540
Kimi no hitomi ni wa

00:20.540 --> 00:21.750
Nadja,

00:20.540 --> 00:21.750
NAAJA

00:21.790 --> 00:24.040
What do you see?

00:21.790 --> 00:24.040
Nani ga mieru

00:24.080 --> 00:26.960
Shining in the far distance,

00:24.080 --> 00:26.960
Haruka tooku hikaru

00:26.960 --> 00:29.340
The door to the future,

00:26.960 --> 00:29.340
Mirai no tobira

00:30.260 --> 00:33.720
That's what I'm searching for

00:30.260 --> 00:33.720
Sagashite iru

00:33.720 --> 00:40.930
Tomorrow's Nadja

00:41.640 --> 00:45.140
If everyone could meet with a smile

00:41.640 --> 00:45.140
Minna egao de aetara

00:45.230 --> 00:48.480
I'm sure there would be no more fighting

00:45.230 --> 00:48.480
Arasoi mo kitto nakunaru

00:48.520 --> 00:51.730
It could be so much more fun

00:48.520 --> 00:51.730
Konna ni mo tanoshi kunaru

00:51.780 --> 00:55.200
The world is wide, but it's still one

00:51.780 --> 00:55.200
Sekai wa hiroi kedo hitotsu ne

00:55.570 --> 00:58.870
I can't see the end of the journey

00:55.570 --> 00:58.870
Tabi no owari wa mienai

00:58.990 --> 01:02.330
God is the only one who could possibly know

00:58.990 --> 01:02.330
Kamisama ga tabun shitteru

01:02.500 --> 01:06.080
To the people who, someday, I will meet again

01:02.500 --> 01:06.080
Itsukamata deaeru hito tachi ni

01:06.120 --> 01:08.250
I will go waving

01:06.120 --> 01:08.250
Te wo furinagara

01:08.330 --> 01:15.010
Sometimes, there are days I feel blue,

01:08.330 --> 01:15.010
Toki ni wa BURUU ni naru hi mo aru kedo

01:15.050 --> 01:17.760
But I won't look back

01:15.050 --> 01:17.760
Ushiro mukanai

01:18.090 --> 01:23.060
Until the day my dream comes true

01:18.090 --> 01:23.060
Yume ga kanau hi made

01:23.350 --> 01:26.770
Nadja, Your smile

01:23.350 --> 01:26.770
NAAJA kimi no hohoemi wa

01:26.850 --> 01:30.190
Nadja, gives me courage

01:26.850 --> 01:30.190
NAAJA yuuki ni naru

01:30.230 --> 01:33.150
Under the blue sky,

01:30.230 --> 01:33.150
Aoi sora no shita de

01:33.280 --> 01:36.110
I will find the place

01:33.280 --> 01:36.110
Ashita no yukue

01:36.400 --> 01:40.330
where my future lies

01:36.400 --> 01:40.330
Mitsukeru kara

01:57.700 --> 01:58.950
﻿Lord Herman..

01:59.110 --> 02:01.820
﻿We've had word from the Director of the Applefield Orphanage...

02:02.120 --> 02:04.990
﻿It seems that Nadja has left Switzerland for Italy...

02:05.500 --> 02:10.500
﻿For the time being, we will go from Paris to Italy's northern gateway, Milan...

02:15.170 --> 02:18.630
﻿Father, happy birthday.

02:19.430 --> 02:21.590
﻿I don't remember inviting you!

02:21.600 --> 02:27.640
﻿Go home! Go home... Go home... Go home...

02:31.520 --> 02:33.110
﻿Just wait, old man...

02:33.110 --> 02:35.270
﻿I will find Nadja no matter what.

02:35.320 --> 02:38.240
﻿And, I'll take the ring that is the only proof

02:38.240 --> 02:40.700
﻿that she has the blood, of the ducal House of Preminger...

02:48.390 --> 02:53.360
Love and Ambition in Milan

03:05.470 --> 03:08.970
﻿Today is the last day of the Dandelion Troupe's Milan performances!

03:09.270 --> 03:15.270
﻿This is the last time you will be able to see... Nadja and Kennosuke's Italian Flag Show!

04:11.460 --> 04:14.500
﻿So, did you find out where Nadja is?

04:14.500 --> 04:17.080
﻿We only arrived the day before yesterday...

04:17.090 --> 04:18.500
﻿And, this is our first time in Milan...

04:19.170 --> 04:20.670
﻿I'm sick of your excuses!

04:20.800 --> 04:22.210
﻿Useless louts!

04:22.220 --> 04:23.920
﻿I-I'm sorry, sir...

04:24.180 --> 04:29.720
﻿You guys just don't understand... how important,the ring inside Nadja’s brooch is...

04:29.720 --> 04:31.810
﻿That's why you can speak so easily!

04:34.480 --> 04:36.850
﻿What is that ring?

04:37.110 --> 04:37.690
﻿It is...

04:37.860 --> 04:38.860
﻿It is?

04:39.610 --> 04:41.360
﻿...none of your business.

04:41.530 --> 04:44.150
﻿Anyway, the first order of business is to find Nadja!

04:44.650 --> 04:45.700
﻿Y-Yes, sir...

04:47.200 --> 04:48.990
﻿Thank you, everyone!

04:49.580 --> 04:51.910
﻿I hope you'll come see us again... the next time we are in Milan that is.

04:54.830 --> 04:56.250
﻿Goodbye!

05:04.930 --> 05:06.680
﻿Why aren't we at the hotel yet?

05:07.140 --> 05:08.220
﻿We've come all the way to Milan...

05:08.300 --> 05:11.510
﻿It would be a shame to leave without seeing the famous Duomo...

05:11.520 --> 05:13.220
﻿So, I took the scenic route.

05:14.430 --> 05:16.190
﻿I didn't come here for sightseeing!

05:16.190 --> 05:17.190
﻿Don't waste my time!

05:17.650 --> 05:19.980
﻿I'm sorry, sir... we'll head for the hotel, right away!

05:35.120 --> 05:37.620
﻿Looks like they were really hungry!

05:37.830 --> 05:40.920
﻿Today's performance was better than usual!

05:42.880 --> 05:47.170
﻿I didn't think that the Milan performances would turn out so well.

05:47.180 --> 05:49.300
﻿So many people, day after day!

05:49.300 --> 05:51.300
﻿Italians are fun-loving people, aren't they.

05:51.470 --> 05:54.470
﻿So, maybe our fun performances were just right for them!

05:54.640 --> 05:57.600
﻿But, I'm a little fed up with the Italian men.

05:57.940 --> 06:00.190
They ask me out before they say hello!

06:00.810 --> 06:02.900
﻿Oh, well, my little Rosebud...

06:02.980 --> 06:05.070
﻿This is the country that created Leonardo, after all.

06:05.070 --> 06:06.740
﻿Don't call me that.

06:06.780 --> 06:09.320
My little Rosebud~!

06:09.320 --> 06:09.860
﻿Kennosuke!

06:09.990 --> 06:11.450
﻿Little Rosebud!

06:11.600 --> 06:13.640
My little Rosebud~!

06:11.620 --> 06:12.990
Stop!

06:12.990 --> 06:14.450
﻿I said stop it!

06:15.080 --> 06:18.370
﻿So, Master, are we leaving for Venice tomorrow?

06:18.580 --> 06:20.880
﻿No, we have an extra day...

06:21.290 --> 06:24.380
﻿So, how about we go sightseeing around Milan, everyone?

06:24.800 --> 06:26.760
B-Bravo! I agree!

06:26.970 --> 06:29.010
﻿Of course, everyone else agrees too, right?

06:32.390 --> 06:33.350
﻿Master!

06:33.350 --> 06:34.720
﻿What's the matter Nadja?

06:34.720 --> 06:36.560
﻿If we can have a day off then...

06:36.560 --> 06:38.560
﻿I have something I'd like to do.

06:38.960 --> 06:39.420
Oh?

06:44.020 --> 06:45.820
﻿And, this second person written here?

06:45.900 --> 06:47.190
﻿Let's see.

06:48.650 --> 06:51.280
﻿His name is Victorio Capuletti...

06:51.280 --> 06:53.160
﻿His hair is black and his eyes are grey.

06:53.490 --> 06:55.160
﻿His hair is black...

06:55.790 --> 06:57.830
﻿And, his eyes are grey...

06:58.460 --> 07:00.460
﻿Oh, this is good!

07:00.540 --> 07:02.630
﻿Is there something funny?

07:02.880 --> 07:07.800
﻿She writes, "He likes playing cards more than dancing, gambling may ruin him someday."

07:08.840 --> 07:13.890
﻿This diary is something your mother wrote after she went to her first ball, isn't it?

07:13.890 --> 07:14.640
﻿Yes.

07:14.850 --> 07:18.220
﻿She was probably a little older than you, Nadja...

07:18.220 --> 07:20.730
﻿But, she had good judgment with regards to men.

07:21.100 --> 07:22.810
﻿Wow! I didn't know that!

07:26.230 --> 07:27.360
﻿All right then!

07:27.530 --> 07:30.030
﻿I'm going to get up early tomorrow, and do my best!

07:30.240 --> 07:31.780
﻿Good night, Mr. Abel!

07:32.030 --> 07:33.530
﻿Good night, Nadja.

07:40.710 --> 07:41.960
I'm ﻿off!

07:44.000 --> 07:45.170
﻿Nadja~!

07:45.340 --> 07:46.460
﻿Wait up~!

07:49.340 --> 07:50.300
﻿Kennosuke?

07:53.130 --> 07:53.930
I'll go with you.

07:54.430 --> 07:57.890
﻿Eh? But, weren't you going with the others to go sightseeing around Milan?

07:58.140 --> 07:59.770
﻿I asked the Master where they were going...

07:59.770 --> 08:01.100
﻿and they seem like places that would be crowded.

08:01.770 --> 08:04.020
﻿And I don't like to stand in line.

08:04.150 --> 08:06.020
﻿That's why, I've decided to go with you.

08:06.310 --> 08:07.900
I see... ﻿thank you!

08:14.320 --> 08:17.160
﻿Moving from country to country like this...

08:17.330 --> 08:19.080
﻿What does it mean?

08:19.120 --> 08:20.580
﻿My thinking is...

08:20.790 --> 08:24.460
﻿Nadja has gotten a job working in import/export or trade of some sort...

08:24.960 --> 08:27.920
﻿Or, she's become an apprentice to a musician or an artist...

08:27.920 --> 08:30.550
﻿...and is traveling around here and there.

08:30.760 --> 08:32.260
I ﻿see.

08:32.760 --> 08:34.340
﻿It's done, Lord Herman!

08:34.340 --> 08:35.680
﻿Nadja looks like this.

08:36.300 --> 08:37.640
﻿Let me see.

08:37.850 --> 08:38.890
﻿Yes, sir... here.

08:42.600 --> 08:44.640
﻿You think we ll be able to find Nadja with this picture!?

08:44.640 --> 08:45.690
I-I'm ﻿sorry.

08:45.690 --> 08:47.310
﻿Even the brooch is all wrong

08:50.400 --> 08:52.690
﻿That's why I said I didn't want to do this...

08:54.280 --> 08:55.610
﻿The brooch looks like this.

09:05.710 --> 09:07.370
So﻿, this is the Scala Opera House..

09:10.000 --> 09:13.380
﻿So, how are you going to look for the noble called Capuletti?

09:13.760 --> 09:15.340
Right now, I have zero leads.

09:15.880 --> 09:17.550
Geez,  just like always.

09:17.840 --> 09:19.930
It's okay! We'll be fine somehow!

09:21.640 --> 09:22.810
Ciao~~!

09:24.930 --> 09:26.560
﻿It's little Rosebud.

09:27.060 --> 09:28.100
﻿Kennosuke!

09:31.360 --> 09:34.400
﻿I didn't think I would see you again so soon!

09:34.690 --> 09:36.240
﻿My little Rosebud.

09:37.660 --> 09:39.160
My ﻿name is Nadja.

09:40.740 --> 09:41.700
﻿Nothing...

09:42.580 --> 09:43.990
﻿Anyway, Leonardo...

09:44.000 --> 09:45.580
﻿Why are you here?

09:45.910 --> 09:47.790
﻿My company is near here.

09:47.830 --> 09:50.250
﻿Really... you work?

09:50.420 --> 09:52.250
Hey, hey, don't say it like that.

09:53.920 --> 09:56.420
By the way, I haven't had breakfast yet.

09:56.590 --> 09:58.180
Would you two like to join me?

09:58.180 --> 10:00.760
﻿We've already eaten, and we're in a hurry.

10:01.050 --> 10:04.600
﻿Don't be so cold... you can stay for a cup of coffee, can't you?

10:06.980 --> 10:08.600
﻿Victorio Capuletti?

10:08.870 --> 10:09.580
You know him?

10:10.060 --> 10:12.020
﻿I've heard of that name from somewhere...

10:15.940 --> 10:18.030
﻿He's not a noble I do business with, but...

10:18.490 --> 10:20.950
﻿I've definitely heard of that name before.

10:23.390 --> 10:24.270
Sorry.

10:24.580 --> 10:25.740
﻿I just can't remember.

10:26.330 --> 10:27.200
﻿I see...

10:27.540 --> 10:29.160
Don't be discouraged...

10:29.460 --> 10:31.880
If he's a noble, I think you can find him somehow.

10:32.860 --> 10:33.770
Excuse me.

10:34.300 --> 10:36.550
﻿Please, prepare some writing materials.

10:36.880 --> 10:37.970
Yes, sir.

10:40.490 --> 10:41.490
Anyway...

10:41.640 --> 10:45.140
I've written down the places where nobles gather and the shops they frequent...

10:45.560 --> 10:47.060
I hope that will help

10:47.060 --> 10:48.060
﻿Thank you!

10:48.520 --> 10:50.100
If you still can't find him...

10:50.350 --> 10:52.520
﻿...come back to my office at four o'clock.

10:53.020 --> 10:55.110
﻿I should be finished with work by then.

10:55.210 --> 10:55.920
Yes!

10:56.440 --> 10:58.690
﻿Whoops! Look at the time!

10:58.820 --> 11:01.450
Sorry, Thierry is waiting for me... I have to get going.

11:01.740 --> 11:04.030
﻿Leonardo, thank you for everything.

11:04.830 --> 11:06.410
I'll search this way...

11:06.540 --> 11:07.830
You take that way.

11:10.920 --> 11:13.790
﻿Damn, he's such a hard man to work for.

11:18.760 --> 11:20.720
﻿This is the hotel Edemila.

11:20.930 --> 11:22.680
﻿Let's start here.

11:22.820 --> 11:23.740
All right!

11:29.810 --> 11:31.390
﻿You're fifteen minutes late.

11:31.640 --> 11:33.560
﻿Yeah... I'm sorry, I'm sorry...

11:33.770 --> 11:35.310
﻿And, there's someone waiting for you.

11:35.860 --> 11:37.690
﻿What? Oh...

11:40.900 --> 11:41.650
﻿Yo.

12:08.770 --> 12:11.020
﻿Antonio... why are you here?

12:11.480 --> 12:14.060
﻿It's about that investment I spoke to you about in Como.

12:14.480 --> 12:17.310
﻿Won't you think about it one more time?

12:17.320 --> 12:18.070
﻿If it's about that...

12:18.070 --> 12:19.480
﻿I said no, and I meant it

12:19.860 --> 12:21.440
﻿Never trust a deal that's too good to be true...

12:22.070 --> 12:23.610
﻿It's a motto that's been passed down in my family.

12:23.860 --> 12:25.070
I'm ﻿sorry, but please leave.

12:26.820 --> 12:30.240
﻿Thierry, I met my little Rosebud again today.

12:30.250 --> 12:31.450
﻿Ah, you mean Nadja.

12:32.000 --> 12:33.330
﻿She's in Milan?

12:33.670 --> 12:34.370
﻿Nadja?

12:34.670 --> 12:36.540
﻿I met her by accident just now, but...

12:36.540 --> 12:39.090
﻿She says she's looking for her mother.

12:39.250 --> 12:42.340
﻿Hmmm, but I heard she grew up in an orphanage.

12:42.550 --> 12:44.470
﻿But, it seems she's alive...

12:44.800 --> 12:48.550
﻿She showed me her mother's diary, containing entries of balls she attended.

12:49.010 --> 12:51.140
﻿Eh? A diary of balls?

12:51.520 --> 12:55.190
﻿Then, Nadja's mother might possibly be... a noble?

12:55.190 --> 12:55.890
﻿What...?

12:58.360 --> 13:00.070
﻿Oh, you're still here...

13:00.670 --> 13:01.460
I apologize but...

13:03.110 --> 13:04.030
﻿Antonio!

13:04.030 --> 13:05.650
﻿W-What is it?

13:06.200 --> 13:09.950
﻿Didn't you talk about a noble named Victorio Capuletti once?

13:10.540 --> 13:14.000
﻿Ah... Now that you mention it, there was a count by that name.

13:14.460 --> 13:16.710
﻿He liked to talk big, but...

13:17.000 --> 13:19.130
﻿...he's just a penniless noble who likes to show off.

13:19.630 --> 13:22.170
﻿So... what about Capuletti?

13:23.800 --> 13:25.300
﻿Oh, nothing.

13:25.800 --> 13:28.970
﻿Now, I have to talk to Thierry about business. So let's end it here.

13:29.510 --> 13:31.260
﻿Tsk! Damned rich boy!

13:37.980 --> 13:40.110
﻿That girl's mother is.

13:40.940 --> 13:42.230
﻿...noble, huh?

13:52.290 --> 13:54.790
﻿Now, where should we go next?

13:55.000 --> 13:56.080
﻿Well...

14:01.290 --> 14:02.210
﻿What's wrong?

14:02.960 --> 14:03.800
﻿Nothing, but...

14:04.050 --> 14:06.840
﻿Herman said that Nadja might be an apprentice to an artist...

14:07.340 --> 14:10.760
﻿...and may be traveling to different countries...

14:10.850 --> 14:12.390
﻿Now that you mention it...

14:12.510 --> 14:14.220
﻿But, I'm sure it's not the opera.

14:14.470 --> 14:15.470
﻿Yeah.

14:33.120 --> 14:34.330
﻿There it is. It's that shop.

14:34.330 --> 14:35.950
﻿Okay, let's go.

14:43.090 --> 14:46.800
We haven't had such a customer come in.

14:47.470 --> 14:48.590
﻿Is that so...

14:51.180 --> 14:51.930
﻿Nadja...

14:52.010 --> 14:53.100
I'm not giving up yet!

14:53.100 --> 14:54.720
﻿I've only just started looking!

14:54.720 --> 14:55.760
﻿That's right!

14:55.810 --> 14:56.850
﻿Let's go to the next one.

15:03.940 --> 15:04.940
﻿Ah! It's Thomas.

15:05.070 --> 15:07.360
You're right... I wonder what he's doing?

15:07.740 --> 15:10.650
﻿Where do artists gather?

15:11.780 --> 15:12.820
﻿A gallery maybe?

15:12.870 --> 15:13.950
﻿That makes sense.

15:14.240 --> 15:16.120
﻿Oh! Perfect, there's one right there!

15:18.200 --> 15:19.410
Thomas! What are you doing?

15:19.750 --> 15:21.620
﻿Hm? Ah! Nadja!

15:21.620 --> 15:23.420
﻿Why arce you two here?

15:23.630 --> 15:25.710
﻿We were passing the front of this shop...

15:25.710 --> 15:27.840
﻿...and, we saw you inside.

15:28.170 --> 15:28.880
﻿Where's everybody?

15:29.090 --> 15:30.010
﻿At the art museum.

15:30.380 --> 15:33.180
﻿I'm more interested in this than art.

15:35.220 --> 15:36.810
﻿In this violin?

15:37.850 --> 15:40.770
This is a violin, but not just any violin...

15:41.230 --> 15:43.020
﻿It is a famous violin that was made 200 years ago...

15:43.100 --> 15:45.270
﻿...called a Stradivarius.

15:45.610 --> 15:47.730
﻿That's a real-tongue twister of a name.

15:48.110 --> 15:48.730
﻿No way!

15:49.070 --> 15:51.280
You could buy a castle for that price!

15:51.490 --> 15:54.200
Why does one musical instrument cost that much?

15:54.740 --> 15:58.950
﻿It was made by a genius craftsman named Antonio Stradivari...

15:59.120 --> 16:02.160
﻿But. there are only about 700 of them left in the world...

16:02.670 --> 16:03.920
﻿So, it's very rare and precious.

16:10.050 --> 16:11.340
﻿With a lousy picture like this...

16:11.340 --> 16:13.180
﻿...there's no way we'll find her... damn it!

16:21.980 --> 16:23.350
﻿What the heck! Darn it!

16:23.730 --> 16:25.440
﻿Wow! What a lousy drawing!

16:25.810 --> 16:27.060
﻿But...

16:27.190 --> 16:29.150
﻿Doesn't it look like Nadja somehow?

16:29.480 --> 16:30.110
﻿Let's see...

16:32.450 --> 16:34.200
﻿I don't have a strange looking face like that!

16:38.740 --> 16:39.950
﻿Excuse me, excuse me...

16:43.750 --> 16:45.120
﻿Excuse me, excuse me..

16:48.040 --> 16:50.840
﻿Hey, You ran into me! Pick it up!

16:51.550 --> 16:53.260
﻿Huh? Yes, ma'am!!!

16:53.510 --> 16:55.130
﻿Nothing again...

17:05.060 --> 17:08.310
﻿I'm worn out... I'll leave the rest to you two.

17:09.150 --> 17:09.900
﻿Shut up!

17:09.900 --> 17:11.480
﻿Hurry up and find her!

17:11.480 --> 17:12.530
﻿Y-Yes, sir!!!

17:12.860 --> 17:15.030
Damn them, the useless louts!

17:15.030 --> 17:16.570
﻿Ahhh! Get out of the way! You're in my way!

17:17.870 --> 17:19.240
﻿Hey, that's dangerous!

17:19.240 --> 17:20.740
﻿Are you okay, Kennosuke?

17:21.790 --> 17:24.500
﻿But, just a little closer and  I would have been hit.

17:26.420 --> 17:27.790
﻿Is it four o'clock already?

17:27.880 --> 17:31.500
﻿Come to think of it, Leonardo told us to go by his office at four, didn't he?

17:31.840 --> 17:33.260
﻿Why don't we go?

17:34.550 --> 17:36.550
﻿What! You found him?!!

17:36.970 --> 17:38.220
﻿He is a count.

17:38.720 --> 17:41.050
I ﻿found his address with Thierry's help...

17:41.060 --> 17:42.010
﻿We got it.

17:42.180 --> 17:44.180
﻿Thank you, Leonardo! Thierry!

17:45.430 --> 17:46.230
﻿Come in.

17:48.850 --> 17:50.900
﻿Sir... I went and bought what you asked for.

17:51.320 --> 17:53.230
﻿Is this all right?

17:53.230 --> 17:53.860
﻿Thank you.

17:55.400 --> 17:56.610
﻿My little Cattleya.

17:57.280 --> 17:58.700
Little Cattleya...

18:07.870 --> 18:08.960
﻿It's a present for you.

18:11.460 --> 18:13.340
﻿My little Rosebud.

18:13.710 --> 18:15.050
﻿What beautiful roses.

18:15.260 --> 18:16.300
﻿Thank you.

18:16.880 --> 18:19.300
﻿I guess, this is the way a gentleman should be.

18:19.470 --> 18:21.430
﻿Hhmp! I'm a samurai!

18:21.720 --> 18:24.260
﻿Then, I'll go get the car...

18:24.430 --> 18:25.970
﻿So, please wait in front of the hotel.

18:26.500 --> 18:27.120
Yes.

18:36.110 --> 18:38.030
﻿Welcome back, Lord Herman.

18:38.360 --> 18:39.530
﻿Take care of the carriage.

18:39.530 --> 18:40.570
﻿Understood, sir.

18:50.830 --> 18:51.790
﻿There he is!

19:05.260 --> 19:06.600
﻿What docs this mean...

19:06.680 --> 19:09.140
﻿It doesn't look as if anyone lives here...

19:12.210 --> 19:13.290
Just when I thought...

19:13.310 --> 19:16.070
﻿...I would finally find something about my mother.

19:25.240 --> 19:26.200
﻿Bonjorno.

19:26.200 --> 19:28.160
﻿May I ask you something?

19:28.370 --> 19:31.080
﻿Isn't this the mansion of Count Capuletti?

19:32.670 --> 19:33.500
﻿Yes..

19:33.630 --> 19:36.960
﻿But, it's the "former' mansion to be precise.

19:36.960 --> 19:38.420
﻿Eh... "former"?

19:39.800 --> 19:42.840
﻿Count Capuletti's investments failed...

19:43.220 --> 19:44.590
﻿About three months ago,

19:44.600 --> 19:48.350
﻿the house and the lands were repossessed by the man he owed money to.

19:48.560 --> 19:50.600
﻿Then, the count has moved away?

19:52.560 --> 19:56.560
﻿Although, he comes to look at the house everyday in regret.

19:56.980 --> 19:59.530
﻿Could it be that... you arc Count Capuletti?

19:59.780 --> 20:01.490
﻿Yes, that the fact.

20:01.820 --> 20:03.070
﻿Count Capuletti...

20:03.530 --> 20:05.370
﻿There's something we would like to ask you...

20:08.660 --> 20:11.410
﻿I don't remember meeting any of you before...

20:12.790 --> 20:15.540
﻿My name is Nadja Applefield.

20:15.860 --> 20:16.770
Actually...

20:20.260 --> 20:21.720
﻿...I understand your situation.

20:22.010 --> 20:26.180
﻿But, although I remember the faces of ladies I played cards with...

20:26.180 --> 20:29.560
﻿I don't remember any of my dance partners.

20:29.810 --> 20:31.020
﻿It could be anything...

20:31.140 --> 20:33.560
﻿Can you not remember even a little bit...

20:38.230 --> 20:40.020
﻿I can't help you...

20:40.030 --> 20:41.230
﻿I'm sorry.

20:41.940 --> 20:43.490
﻿Thank you.

20:54.420 --> 20:56.540
﻿Antonio Fabiani...!

20:57.630 --> 21:00.170
﻿If only he had not existed!

21:03.840 --> 21:06.430
﻿Antonio... could it be "that" Antonio?

21:07.760 --> 21:08.930
﻿Here, take it.

21:10.220 --> 21:12.770
﻿Buy a dress or anything else you like.

21:12.980 --> 21:14.680
﻿I don't want your money!

21:15.250 --> 21:15.870
Yeah.

21:16.310 --> 21:19.980
﻿Even though it was risky, he promoted it as a great deal...

21:20.230 --> 21:22.190
﻿...and took everything from him.

21:22.530 --> 21:23.740
﻿That's terrible...

21:31.240 --> 21:32.790
﻿Even though, I didn't find anything today...

21:33.040 --> 21:36.160
﻿If I keep believing, I'll meet her someday!

21:36.710 --> 21:38.290
﻿We'll pray for you from behind the scenes.

21:38.500 --> 21:39.500
﻿Thank you.

21:39.630 --> 21:42.300
﻿Well, see you... my little Rosebud.

21:45.170 --> 21:47.050
﻿I really want to thank you for today.

21:48.590 --> 21:49.340
﻿Those two...

21:49.640 --> 21:51.140
﻿They're nicer than I thought.

21:52.770 --> 21:56.230
﻿Everyone's waiting... let's hurry up and go home. My little Rosebud!

21:58.560 --> 22:00.730
﻿Kennosuke, you wait!

